                        "glosses": [
                            "Synonym of thingy: something one cannot remember the name of, or is unable to or does not care to specify precisely."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "382aa6ff-b030-3774-b90a-30e023d47f07",
                        "entry_id": "ae4b8d1f-ea7a-3789-abb1-2d048aaa61ed",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Synonym of whatshisname: someone one cannot remember the name of."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "52580538-040f-4803-a72f-997c4cf83047",
                                "sense_id": "382aa6ff-b030-3774-b90a-30e023d47f07",
                                "text": "Once, in his first term, Cartwright had been bold enough to ask him why he was so clever, […]\n‘It’s memory, Cartwright, old dear. Memory, the mother of the Muses . . . at least that’s what thingummy said.’\n‘Who?’\n‘You know, what’s his name, Greek poet chap. Wrote the Theogony . . . what was he called? Begins with an “H”.’\n‘Homer?’\n‘No, dear. Not Homer, the other one. No, it’s gone. Anyway. Memory, that’s the key.’"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
